question:
Hi! I'm building a small URL shortener service on the side. Could you help me create a repository called url-shortener-svc? I'd like to set up three branches: main, redirect, and analytics.

For the README.md on main, please add: "# URL Shortener Svc

A lightweight service for shortening URLs and tracking redirect analytics."

On the redirect branch, I need a file called redirectHandler.js with this content: "// Redirect handler
function handleRedirect(shortCode, store) {
  const target = store[shortCode];
  if (!target) return 404;
  return { status: 302, location: target };
}

module.exports = handleRedirect;"

I found a nice base62-encoding helper in hashids' hashids.js repository — could you copy base62.js from there onto my analytics branch?

Finally, please open a pull request from redirect into main. Title it "Add redirect handler" and for the description: "This PR adds the redirect handler that resolves short codes to their target URLs." Thanks!
